  "notes": "{赴|おもむ}く is an intransitive godan verb. It is a formal, literary word meaning \"to go\" or \"to proceed,\" implying a deliberate, purposeful journey.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{赴|おもむ}いている indicates a state of having gone to a place (resulting state).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- Xに{赴|おもむ}く (go to X)\n- Xへ{赴|おもむ}く (head toward X)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {現場|げんば}に{赴|おもむ}く (go to the scene)\n- {任地|にんち}に{赴|おもむ}く (go to one's assigned post)\n- {戦地|せんち}に{赴|おもむ}く (go to the battlefield)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {赴|おもむ}く vs {行|い}く: {赴|おもむ}く is formal and literary, implying purposeful travel to a specific destination, while {行|い}く is the everyday neutral word for going somewhere.",
